@page "/"
<main class="page">
    <section class="hero">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL RESEARCH WORKSPACE · M23</p>
            <h1>Evidence before execution.</h1>
            <p class="hero-copy">Build strategies, replay completed candles, validate them out of sample and inspect the results without giving the research system authority to trade.</p>
            <div class="actions">
                <a class="button primary" href="/reports">Open research reports</a>
                <a class="button secondary" href="/health/ready">Check database readiness</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="principle-card" aria-label="Architecture principle">
            <span>C#</span><strong>calculates</strong>
            <span>SQL</span><strong>preserves evidence</strong>
            <span>AI</span><strong>explains evidence</strong>
            <span>You</span><strong>retain authority</strong>
        </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="status-grid" aria-label="Milestone capabilities">
        <article><span class="card-index">01</span><h2>Replay</h2><p>Completed-candle fills with slippage, dated Indian costs and whole-lot risk sizing.</p></article>
        <article><span class="card-index">02</span><h2>Validate</h2><p>Chronological holdout, walk-forward folds, market regimes and parameter neighborhoods.</p></article>
        <article><span class="card-index">03</span><h2>Rank</h2><p>Evidence-weighted scores with hard qualification gates and at most two selections.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-banner">
        <div><span class="status-dot"></span><strong>M23 semi-live and direct-live gates are ready</strong></div>
        <p>Semi-live produces manual proposals. Direct protected LIMIT entry remains disabled until both local gates and explicit order confirmation are present.</p>
    </section>
</main>
